A resumed thread is made ready but not put on a queue.
It would never get the processor;
every ready thread but the running one that may run waits on a queue.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a ready thread that may run waits on no queue

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -426,7 +426,7 @@ static int op_thread(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, const uint32_t *arg)
         if (target->state != THREAD_STOPPED || thread_process(target) == NULL) {
             return KERR_STATE;
         }
-        sched_ready(target);
+        target->state = THREAD_READY;
         return KERR_OK;
     default:
         return KERR_WRONG_TYPE;
